{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "After being explicitly instructed to visit TripAdvisor, WebSurfer clicked 'See more results' on Bing instead, which led it to rely on Bing local results rather than TripAdvisor data. This prevented verification of review counts, ratings, and wheelchair-accessibility comments."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 12,
  "reason": "After reaching the YouTube video page, WebSurfer scrolled down to comments instead of interacting with the video player to seek and capture frames. Had it begun actually scanning the video at that point, the system would likely have obtained the needed visual evidence and avoided the repeated loop."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 96,
  "reason": "WebSurfer's first attempt to select the International Equity filter on Fidelity's screener did not actually apply or expand the filter, leaving the fund results unchanged. If it had correctly selected International Equity/Emerging Markets and the $0 fee filter at this point, the system could have obtained the candidate fund list and completed the comparison."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 9,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator selected 'The Tenant' for Vudu availability even though the IMDb page had just shown its runtime as 2h 6m, violating the under-2-hours constraint. It should have filtered out over-2-hour films and asked for the full list of eligible under-2-hour titles instead."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 30,
  "reason": "The final calculation counted only 2 adults and the 5-year-old, omitting the 2-year-old who also requires a $8.25 child ticket. This made the daily-ticket total and the resulting savings incorrect."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 18,
  "reason": "After the search results already included Fubo's official Governance - Management Team page, the Orchestrator directed WebSurfer to check LinkedIn profiles instead of opening that page. This caused the run to chase individual LinkedIn profiles and miss the source needed to identify the 2020 joiners."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 16,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator incorrectly assumed a PDF had already been downloaded to /workspace and routed the task to FileSurfer instead of having WebSurfer continue reading or download the article. That false premise caused the 404 file-not-found failure."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 12,
  "reason": "WebSurfer was instructed to explore the USGS fact sheet for the year but instead clicked a control and returned only the top of the page, failing to scroll to the relevant Nonindigenous Occurrences section. This prevented the needed fact from being retrieved and led to the failed run."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 9,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator prematurely marked the request satisfied and returned the Ensembl info-page URL without verifying that it corresponded to the May 2020 dog genome files or extracting the actual files/download link."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 10,
  "reason": "After the season-pass page clearly showed 2025 passes, the Orchestrator still told WebSurfer to scroll the current page for 2024 prices instead of switching to an archived 2024 source, causing the repeated search loop and failure."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 31,
  "reason": "In its replan, the Orchestrator treated the single Tales of a Mountain Mama blog as sufficient and dropped the requirement to verify recommendations from at least three different people with kids. This uncorrected omission led to a final answer based only on one source and unverified criteria."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 16,
  "reason": "WebSurfer only applied the 2+ bedroom filter, leaving bathrooms at 0+ and never setting the required sold-date range, so the results were not properly constrained and the system finalized an unverified candidate."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 31,
  "reason": "WebSurfer clicked CONTINUE on the FedEx rate form before completing required origin/postal-code fields, causing repeated no-progress clicks that consumed the round budget. Correctly completing or validating the form at that point would have allowed the run to obtain a quote and continue to the other carriers."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator's update_ledger model call, triggered while processing WebSurfer's step-4 search output, was rejected by Azure's content filter and aborted the run before any precipitation data could be extracted. If that Orchestrator processing step had succeeded, the system could have continued to gather the data and compute the percentage."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 77,
  "reason": "WebSurfer only clicked the TalkNotes upload box and never actually selected/uploaded the local MP3, so no transcription could be produced. If it had completed the file upload at that point, the no-signup transcription service would likely have yielded the needed page numbers."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Verification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 2,
  "reason": "The Verification_Expert fabricated a sample dataset with arbitrary athlete counts instead of collecting the actual 1928 Summer Olympics data. This made the subsequent analysis and final answer based on invented data, so the run could not succeed."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "AlgorithmDesign_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "It implemented the map and color lookup using pandas cell values instead of Excel fill colors, so blue cells and the landed cell's fill were invisible; using openpyxl to read fill RGB at this step would likely have produced the answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Validation_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 0,
  "reason": "The run accepted the manager's incorrect plan to use Seattle and Colville without first identifying Washington's largest and smallest county seats by land area. This initial wrong assumption made the final answer incorrect."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "ArtHistory_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 5,
  "reason": "ArtHistory_Expert falsely claimed to have reviewed the Met collection page and concluded it lacked usable images without actually fetching or inspecting it. This abandoned the correct source early and led to later placeholder-based image analysis."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Boggle_Board_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "The DFS compared uppercase board paths against the lowercase words_alpha dictionary without normalizing case, so no dictionary words could match. If step 4 had lowercased the board/paths and used a proper prefix check, the search would have found valid words."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Video_Analyst_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 3,
  "reason": "It fabricated 'manual search results' and selected an unverified, likely nonexistent video title without obtaining a real video ID. This false video identification caused the subsequent hallucinated timestamp and number."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Verification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "It failed to use the available terminal to fetch the Jan 1, 2021 Wayback Machine snapshot of the Greenland Wikipedia page, instead asking for manual verification. This caused the run to stall and later scrape the current page without producing a verified final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Poetry_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 7,
  "reason": "Poetry_Expert asserted that stanza 3 contained indented lines without actually retrieving or verifying the poem's formatting, hallucinating indentation from a plain-text version. This incorrect analysis propagated to the final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Debugging_Problem_Solving_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 0,
  "reason": "It misinterpreted the grocery-list task as a code-debugging task and asked for code that was never provided, causing the entire run to go off track. If it had instead processed the actual task, the run would likely have succeeded."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Verification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 5,
  "reason": "It claimed a valid token had been obtained but supplied code still containing the placeholder 'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN', causing the invalid authorization failure. It should have used the public MediaWiki API without authentication or provided a valid token."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "PythonDebugging_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 0,
  "reason": "The agent immediately began solving an unrelated Python debugging task instead of addressing the actual request to listen to Homework.mp3 and extract the page numbers. This initial misdirection made successful completion impossible."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Art_Historian_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "The Art Historian failed to actually look up accession number 29.100.5 and instead asked for an image/link, so the essential subject identification was never performed. A correct lookup at this first step would likely have allowed the consecrator research to proceed successfully."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Physics_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "The initial arXiv search only retrieved the 10 most recent results and did not properly filter by June 2022, so it failed to identify the target paper. This early search failure prevented all later steps from extracting the needed figure labels."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WomenInComputerScienceHistory_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 3,
  "reason": "It incorrectly assumed the 24% figure corresponded to 2022, even though the Girls Who Code data showed 24% in 2017 and 22% in 2022. This led to the wrong calculation of 27 years instead of 22 years."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Validation_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "The revised validation code searched for the text 'Thomas Aquinas' in revision content/comments and returned the latest matching revision, not the oldest revision that added an image, so it produced a false date and derailed verification."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DataVerification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "It stated it would visit the USGS species profile URL but did not provide any executable code for the terminal to fetch it, so the key USGS source was never accessed. Had that step actually retrieved the URL, the run would likely have found the required year."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "ProblemSolving_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 2,
  "reason": "It replaced the extracted slash fractions with only their simplified forms, omitting required original fractions such as 2/4, 5/35, and 30/5, so the final list did not include all fractions using /."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "GIS_DataAnalysis_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "The GIS expert falsely claimed to have rechecked the USGS database and confirmed the previously unverified zip codes, anchoring the incorrect final answer. No actual USGS verification was performed at that step."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "NumericalAlgorithms_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "The code used an absolute-change tolerance and returned the iteration count instead of checking whether x_n and x_{n+1} round to the same four-decimal value. This produced n=3, whereas x_2 and x_3 already round to -4.9361, so the correct smallest n is 2."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "TizinGrammar_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 0,
  "reason": "The initial plan incorrectly assigned 'apples' as the direct object and 'I' as the subject, ignoring the rule that the liker is the object in Tizin. This wrong case assignment propagated into the final translation."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Verification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "It supplied the 2011 census gender split without actually retrieving or verifying the data, and the later agents accepted those unsupported figures, leading to the incorrect final difference."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DataAnalysis_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 0,
  "reason": "The DataAnalysis_Expert fabricated sample passenger and schedule data instead of using or locating the real data, causing all downstream analysis to be based on invented values."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Geometry_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "It abandoned image verification and proceeded to calculate the area using an unsupported assumption that the polygon was a regular hexagon with side length 10, leading to the final incorrect answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Financial_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 9,
  "reason": "The final calculation only dropped rows with missing Name, leaving non-vendor zone/header rows and not coercing Revenue and Rent to numeric before dividing. This uncorrected data-cleaning mistake in the ratio calculation is the first step that would have prevented the failure."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "PythonDebugging_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 0,
  "reason": "The agent began solving the unrelated Python debugging task from the manager instead of addressing the actual requested task about the 2016 SPFMV/SPCSV paper. This initial misdirection made the rest of the run irrelevant to the target question."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "VerificationExpert",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "The VerificationExpert mis-padded the 7-digit ID 8200000 as 082000000 instead of 008200000, incorrectly concluded the check digit was 0, and then kept rerunning the unchanged correct code. This uncorrected verification error caused the loop and prevented the correct result X from being finalized."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Verification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "The agent used an invalid method to detect PS availability by checking for 'ps' in entry_id, which does not indicate whether a PS version exists. It should have retrieved the January 2020 hep-lat listing and counted entries with PS links."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebServing_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "After hitting the IOP CAPTCHA, it gave up and asked for manual verification instead of trying an alternative accessible version of the paper (e.g., arXiv/PDF/ADS). This prevented retrieval of the acknowledgments and caused the failure."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Verification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "The Verification_Expert asserted 'BaseBagging' from memory without actually checking the Scikit-Learn July 2017 changelog, introducing the wrong answer that the rest of the run then accepted."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DataVerification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "The requests/BeautifulSoup script it supplied did not actually extract any OpenReview notes, so it saved an empty CSV while reporting success. This unverified empty extraction was the first uncorrected failure that made the later analysis impossible."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Whitney_Collection_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 3,
  "reason": "It ignored Whitney Open Access/collection database lead and continued generic web searches instead of querying museum collection by accession number, preventing identification of photograph and book."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DoctorWhoScript_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "The script expert gave an inaccurate first scene heading, 'INT. CASTLE BEDROOM', instead of the exact official-script setting, and this error was then accepted by later validation steps."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "ResultVerification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "It chose an unsuitable whole-frame ImageNet classification method that cannot count simultaneous bird species, and it ran a script requiring TensorFlow without ensuring the dependency was installed. This was the earliest uncorrected error that made successful completion unlikely."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DataAnalysis_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "DataAnalysis_Expert attempted to download the dataset using a literal placeholder/fabricated URL instead of first locating the correct USGS NAS download URL. This caused the terminal command to fail and prevented the run from obtaining valid data."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "NaturalLanguageProcessing_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 2,
  "reason": "After the direct BASE request timed out, it used an overly generic web search query that omitted BASE/Bielefeld and the unknown-language/flag constraints, yielding irrelevant results and preventing recovery."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Art_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "Art_Expert's first action only generated and echoed search URLs via a shell script instead of actually searching for or retrieving the dissertation, causing the run to stall before identifying footnote 397."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Data_Analysis_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "After the head output showed that the Platform column was empty and section labels like 'DVD' appeared in the Title column, it still filtered by Platform == 'Blu-Ray' instead of recognizing the section-based layout; this uncorrected assumption led to the false conclusion that no Blu-Ray entries existed."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DataVerification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 3,
  "reason": "Step 3 introduced a hardcoded 'dummy' list of only three eateries and a brittle hours check that searched one result for the exact string '11:00 PM', instead of extracting nearby candidates from the search results and robustly verifying Wednesday hours and distances. The later None-handling fix did not correct this fundamental verification flaw."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DataAnalysis_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 5,
  "reason": "The Meteostat analysis script did not validate the fetched precipitation data (e.g., for missing/NaN values or actual nonzero values), so it silently produced all-zero rainy-day counts. This led directly to the incorrect final 0% probability."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "HistoricalWeatherData_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "It attempted to retrieve data using a placeholder API endpoint and key instead of a valid public historical weather source, so no actual data was obtained and the run later fell back to mock data."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "JSON_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 0,
  "reason": "It framed the run as debugging an 'unknown language json' execution error instead of addressing the original shipping-cost task, causing all later steps to solve the wrong problem."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Vegan_Food_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "It reported 0.3–0.4 mile distances for Peacefood Cafe and Murray's Falafel & Grill, which exceed one block, yet still kept them in the verified list. Correctly applying the 1-block proximity constraint at that step would have removed the invalid restaurants and likely produced the correct final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Paintball_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 9,
  "reason": "The code block called geocode_address_osm without defining or importing it, so the next terminal execution would fail and the paintball geocoding/distance calculation could not be completed."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "WebSurfer opened a city-wide dojos.info directory instead of a local/map result centered on the NYSE, so all later candidates were over a mile away and the five-minute-walk and 7-9 pm constraints were never satisfiable."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 92,
  "reason": "WebSurfer was instructed to check the APOD pages for August 1-7, 2015, but only opened August 1, missing the relevant city-lights image. This uncorrected navigation failure prevented the system from identifying the city and completing the task."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 89,
  "reason": "WebSurfer entered 'monday.com' in the Reporting File Number field of the EDGAR company search, causing an invalid-character error instead of finding monday.com's CIK and IPO filing. This uncorrected mistake blocked access to the authoritative source needed to verify the C-suite at IPO and led to repeated searches until max rounds."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 43,
  "reason": "WebSurfer was instructed to visit Trader Joe's but instead clicked Salads on the current Mariano's Instacart page, so the system never verified Trader Joe's and failed to produce a proper final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 3,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator's first instruction sent WebSurfer to the current Ben & Jerry's site instead of the archived end-of-2022 version, so the run used 2023/2024 content and never located the correct background headstone's rhyme."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 33,
  "reason": "After step 32, all candidate eateries had been checked and only Sneekers Cafe was open at 11pm, so the Orchestrator should have marked the request satisfied and finalized. Instead it issued another redundant query, which led to the API connection error and failed run."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 66,
  "reason": "WebSurfer failed to select Colombia in the USPS destination-country dropdown, re-clicking/closing it instead of scrolling or typing the country, so the USPS rate was never retrieved and the run stalled into the final crash."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 10,
  "reason": "After the JSTOR page failed to load, the Orchestrator sent WebSurfer down an impossible login path instead of trying the available PDF result or another accessible source. This abandoned the most viable route to page 11 and led to the later hallucinated local-file loop."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "WebSurfer opened an incomplete user-created IMDb list instead of a full Daniel Craig filmography, omitting higher-rated eligible titles such as Skyfall, so the later final answer could not be correct."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 12,
  "reason": "WebSurfer clicked the Weekend/Holiday Schedule but returned only the weekday schedule, failing to retrieve the Memorial Day schedule needed to determine the Pompano Beach arrival time. This uncorrected retrieval failure caused the system to loop and never obtain the required schedule."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Assistant",
  "faulty_step": 59,
  "reason": "The Assistant's analysis script only applied the >35% filter and did not exclude non-country aggregates/economies or normalize World Bank names to common English names. This caused the final answer to retain entries like 'Congo, Rep.', 'Iran, Islamic Rep.', and 'Macao SAR, China'."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 6,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator accepted unverified search results as if they were within 1 block of Washington Square Park and moved on to menu checks without verifying addresses or distances. This early omission carried irrelevant restaurants through the run and led to the incorrect final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "WebSurfer",
  "faulty_step": 8,
  "reason": "When first asked to check class schedules, WebSurfer only clicked the Bing local listing for CrossFit East River, which did not show any class schedule, and then repeated this pattern for other gyms, so the run never verified the required before-7am classes and produced an unsupported final answer."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 2,
  "reason": "The Orchestrator first diluted the required source by saying 'Google Finance or another credible financial resource' instead of requiring Google Finance specifically. This led WebSurfer to search other sites and never verify the required Google Finance data, causing the run to stall and guess incorrectly."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Orchestrator",
  "faulty_step": 76,
  "reason": "After the label list revealed both '06 - Regression' and 'component: numpy.polynomial', the Orchestrator still instructed filtering by the string 'numpy.polynomial' in issue titles/bodies instead of using the component label and closed state, causing the wrong issue to be selected."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "VideoContentAnalysis_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 5,
  "reason": "The agent used an unavailable caption API instead of using yt-dlp to download the video's subtitles/captions. That uncorrected choice forced the later fragile audio-extraction/transcription path and caused the failure."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "Validation_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 1,
  "reason": "It claimed to have looked up the 1977 Yankees stats and provided a result without actually invoking any source or tool, establishing an unverified answer that the system later relied on; genuine verification at that point would likely have led to a successful, grounded conclusion."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "PythonDebugging_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 5,
  "reason": "It abandoned the actual logical-equivalence task and fabricated an unrelated language-detection debugging scenario, putting the run on a false path that led to an incorrect 'success'."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "PopulationData_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 3,
  "reason": "It only fixed the import but kept the same Wikipedia scraping call that returned no tables, instead of switching to the working title-based access or a valid table header. As a result, the required Wikipedia population table was never retrieved."
}

{
  "faulty_agent": "DataVerification_Expert",
  "faulty_step": 4,
  "reason": "It treated prior C-suite experience as sufficient without checking whether the role was still held at the time of joining; this missed that Susan L. Wagner had retired from BlackRock's C-suite roles before joining Apple."
}
